141	/**
142	 * The late charge on a claim: an OPEN (or PENDING) claim whose due-by (fixed when it was created) is before
143	 * the sheet's today gains, for each full 30 days it is overdue, the sheet's late percent in force on that
144	 * boundary date (its due-by plus 30, 60, 90 ... days) of its figure plus the charges of the boundaries before it
145	 * (compounding), each rounded like due, the charges added up
146	 * (a boundary whose percent is 0.00 adds nothing); a deferred claim is not overdue. A correction has no late charge. The charge is never bound by a statement; settling freezes it in.
147	 * The charge is worked on the rate figure alone (or the figure a statement bound); the floor is applied last.
148	 * With grace days (those of its person's grade in force on its date) the claim is overdue only once its due-by plus them is
149	 * before today, and the 30-day boundaries are counted from its due-by plus them.
150	 */
